WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.476 --> 00:00:07.258
"No way!

2
00:00:07.698 --> 00:00:18.902
Who would slash our bike tires?"

3
00:00:19.403 --> 00:00:21.624
Maggie cried, rushing over to her bicycle.

4
00:00:26.205 --> 00:00:26.706
she added.

5
00:00:26.726 --> 00:00:29.107
"I think my tires are okay."

6
00:00:29.127 --> 00:00:32.168
"Mine too," someone else called out.

7
00:00:33.164 --> 00:00:34.265
Henry checked his bike.

8
00:00:34.925 --> 00:00:36.126
His tires were fine.

9
00:00:36.146 --> 00:00:40.328
"It looks like only some tires were slashed," he said.

10
00:00:40.348 --> 00:00:43.310
"Yeah. Like mine!"

11
00:00:43.690 --> 00:00:46.152
Cole sounded upset as he looked at his tires.

12
00:00:46.172 --> 00:00:49.334
"Who would be mean enough to do this?"

13
00:00:49.354 --> 00:00:52.195
"I don't know," Henry said.

14
00:00:52.215 --> 00:00:55.857
"But maybe The Lemonade Detectives can figure it out."

15
00:00:56.858 --> 00:01:00.140
He looked around, trying to see how everyone was reacting.

16
00:01:01.064 --> 00:01:03.526
Most of the riders looked confused or upset.

17
00:01:04.386 --> 00:01:06.327
A bunch of kids were gathered around Ms.

18
00:01:06.347 --> 00:01:09.489
Hernandez, asking her questions about what had happened.

19
00:01:11.890 --> 00:01:14.512
Then Henry spotted the man in the dark glasses.

20
00:01:15.472 --> 00:01:18.714
He was standing by his bike with his arms folded, looking bored.

21
00:01:19.675 --> 00:01:20.835
Maggie noticed him too.

22
00:01:20.855 --> 00:01:23.797
"Hey, maybe it was that guy!"

23
00:01:24.217 --> 00:01:24.938
she whispered.

24
00:01:24.958 --> 00:01:28.480
"I didn't see him while we were at the picnic spot.

25
00:01:29.364 --> 00:01:32.106
He could have been down here slashing tires the whole time!"

26
00:01:32.126 --> 00:01:34.628
"Maybe," Henry said.

27
00:01:34.648 --> 00:01:37.389
"I didn't notice him while we were up there either."

28
00:01:37.409 --> 00:01:41.672
"I bet it was those kids from Valley High School," said Cole.

29
00:01:41.692 --> 00:01:45.275
"They probably came on the ride to make trouble!"

30
00:01:46.115 --> 00:01:48.397
Henry looked around for the Valley High teens.

31
00:01:49.437 --> 00:01:53.100
He couldn't see the girl in the crowd, but he spotted the boy right away.

32
00:01:54.040 --> 00:01:56.862
He was smirking as he watched everyone check their tires.

33
00:01:56.882 --> 00:02:00.036
"His tires look okay," Cole said.

34
00:02:00.056 --> 00:02:02.978
"And we already know he doesn't like Belltown.

35
00:02:03.638 --> 00:02:05.359
Remember how he was teasing Nathan?"

36
00:02:05.379 --> 00:02:09.921
"Yeah. He should be a suspect too," Henry said.

37
00:02:09.941 --> 00:02:12.902
"Did anyone see him at the picnic area?"

38
00:02:12.922 --> 00:02:15.543
"I didn't," Maggie said.

39
00:02:15.563 --> 00:02:17.204
"So that proves it!

40
00:02:17.264 --> 00:02:18.265
He's guilty!"

41
00:02:19.245 --> 00:02:21.906
As usual, Maggie was jumping to conclusions.

42
00:02:21.926 --> 00:02:25.548
"It doesn't prove anything," Henry reminded her.

43
00:02:26.520 --> 00:02:30.081
"There were lots of people I didn't notice while we were at the picnic area.

44
00:02:30.882 --> 00:02:34.703
We should start questioning everyone and see who left."

45
00:02:34.803 --> 00:02:36.504
"I remember someone who left!"

46
00:02:36.944 --> 00:02:37.544
Maggie said.

47
00:02:37.564 --> 00:02:39.905
"That rich kid, William.

48
00:02:40.686 --> 00:02:43.507
I saw him get up and walk toward the path leading down here."

49
00:02:44.667 --> 00:02:47.448
Henry remembered seeing William leave the picnic area too.

50
00:02:47.468 --> 00:02:49.689
"Okay," he said.

51
00:02:49.709 --> 00:02:52.270
"But that doesn't prove anything either.

52
00:02:53.271 --> 00:02:55.872
Lots of people left to walk down to the restrooms."

53
00:02:56.788 --> 00:02:58.809
Just then Jill and Ashley rushed over.

54
00:02:58.829 --> 00:03:01.009
"This is terrible!"

55
00:03:01.329 --> 00:03:02.050
Ashley cried.

56
00:03:02.070 --> 00:03:05.230
"Someone's trying to ruin our fundraiser!"

57
00:03:05.250 --> 00:03:08.291
"You have to help us," Jill added.

58
00:03:08.311 --> 00:03:12.432
"We want to hire The Lemonade Detectives to solve this horrible crime!"

59
00:03:13.893 --> 00:03:14.773
Henry smiled.

60
00:03:14.793 --> 00:03:18.914
"I don't know if I'd call it a horrible crime," he said.

61
00:03:18.934 --> 00:03:21.735
"But don't worry.

62
00:03:22.295 --> 00:03:23.756
We're already on the case.

63
00:03:24.456 --> 00:03:26.857
To start, we want to question you two."

64
00:03:26.877 --> 00:03:29.798
"What?" Jill looked outraged.

65
00:03:30.438 --> 00:03:32.839
"You don't suspect us again, do you?"

66
00:03:32.859 --> 00:03:35.661
"No!" Henry said quickly.

67
00:03:35.681 --> 00:03:38.282
"You're not suspects this time."

68
00:03:39.142 --> 00:03:40.483
He knew why Jill was annoyed.

69
00:03:41.503 --> 00:03:46.025
Somehow she ended up being a suspect in a lot of The Lemonade Detectives' cases.

70
00:03:47.126 --> 00:03:48.906
Ashley had been a suspect once too.

71
00:03:49.547 --> 00:03:52.168
Henry was pretty sure that they were innocent again now.

72
00:03:53.076 --> 00:03:55.738
Why would they try to ruin a fundraiser for their own team?

73
00:03:55.758 --> 00:03:58.279
"So what do you want to ask us?"

74
00:03:58.699 --> 00:03:59.440
Ashley asked.

75
00:04:00.320 --> 00:04:02.301
"Do you know how many bikes got damaged?"

76
00:04:02.722 --> 00:04:03.522
Henry asked.

77
00:04:04.503 --> 00:04:05.303
Ashley shrugged.

78
00:04:05.983 --> 00:04:08.165
"We're not sure exactly," she said.

79
00:04:08.185 --> 00:04:11.306
"We'll have to check with Ms.

80
00:04:11.326 --> 00:04:15.809
Hernandez. But at least six or seven bikes have slashed tires."

81
00:04:15.829 --> 00:04:20.852
"We were just trying to figure out who left the picnic spot," Cole added.

82
00:04:21.688 --> 00:04:23.309
"Did you notice anyone slipping away?"

83
00:04:23.329 --> 00:04:28.192
"Oh." Jill looked less upset now that she realized she wasn't a suspect.

84
00:04:28.212 --> 00:04:29.652
"I don't know.

85
00:04:29.672 --> 00:04:31.874
I wasn't paying much attention to that."

86
00:04:31.894 --> 00:04:34.175
"Yeah," Ashley said.

87
00:04:34.195 --> 00:04:37.297
"I walked down to the restrooms with a couple of friends.

88
00:04:38.637 --> 00:04:41.419
The only person there when we left was your friend Nathan."

89
00:04:42.640 --> 00:04:46.242
Henry nodded, remembering that Nathan had gone to the restroom alone.

90
00:04:47.182 --> 00:04:49.904
He was sure his friend hadn't slashed those tires.

91
00:04:50.860 --> 00:04:53.202
But maybe Nathan had seen something suspicious.

92
00:04:53.222 --> 00:04:55.584
"Thanks," Henry said.

93
00:04:55.604 --> 00:04:58.106
"We'd better start investigating.

94
00:04:58.846 --> 00:05:00.388
What are you going to do about the ride?"

95
00:05:00.408 --> 00:05:02.089
"Good question."

96
00:05:02.650 --> 00:05:04.611
Cole frowned as he looked at his bike again.

97
00:05:04.631 --> 00:05:07.333
"I can't ride with a slashed tire."

98
00:05:07.353 --> 00:05:08.854
"I think Ms.

99
00:05:08.894 --> 00:05:10.936
Hernandez is calling Belltown Bikes."

100
00:05:12.537 --> 00:05:15.980
Ashley glanced over at the coach, who was talking on her cell phone.

101
00:05:16.000 --> 00:05:20.544
"She's going to ask them to bring new tires to replace the slashed ones."

102
00:05:21.760 --> 00:05:23.041
"Good," Henry said.

103
00:05:23.061 --> 00:05:27.105
"That should give us some time to question people before the ride continues."

104
00:05:27.125 --> 00:05:30.288
"Yeah." Jill didn't look happy.

105
00:05:30.308 --> 00:05:33.051
"But someone will have to pay for the new tires.

106
00:05:33.812 --> 00:05:38.116
So if you guys don't solve the mystery, we might not raise enough money to buy our uniforms!"
